  "visualBrief": "Principal Montreal limestone Gothic Revival basilica: twin square65m towers with paired lancets,louvres,rose windows,octagonal corner colonnettes,crenels and eight slender pinnacle tips; deeply recessed triple entrance portico,three statuary niches with robed saints,blind pointed arcade and central cross; low-pitched copper main roof,four wide transomed nave bays per side,raised rear end bay,roofline pinnacles,lower masonry,basement entrance canopy and raised east-tower door/stair. Native western low projection remains estimated. Rear Sacred Heart chapel,adjacent seminary,interiors,scaffolding,banners and street scenery excluded.",
